We thank the reviewers for their time and feedback. 

From the reviews, it is clear that more detail on practical and theoretical considerations could enhance the rigor and quality of our work. We have therefore strived to address this in the revised manuscript. In particular, we have added discussion on:

1. Scaling Koopman pruning up to larger DNNs (R2);

2. Contrasting Koopman mode decomposition with other linearization methods (R3);

3. Using Koopman mode decomposition in regimes where the parameter dynamics are not linear (R4); 

4. Interpreting the Koopman magnitude pruning results in the pre-convergence phase of training (R4).  

More detail on each of these points, and additional questions that were raised, can be found in the responses to each reviewer and the revised manuscript.
